y Pocket the iPhone classic kit  and the Nintendo classic kit frames and  since it's Grid's two-year anniversary  those ordering between now and the 11th  could win limited edition prices like  the iPad 1 or MacBook airframes a  special badge collection or a t-shirt so  check out the link below now getting  back to what makes the Apple watch Ultra  so special the extreme weatherproof  design allowing it to maintain proper  operation in environments ranging from  negative 4 degrees to 131 degrees  Fahrenheit helping it achieve its 810 H  military standard rating which yes is  used by the military to make sure their  gear can handle extreme environments and  on top of that it's water resistant  rated up to the en 13319 diving standard  which is basically the highest rating  for snorkeling high-speed water sports  and scuba diving all the way down to 130  feet below the surface coming with both  a depth gauge and a water temperature  sensor which is really cool as well as  the exclusive Oceanic plus diving app  making it a certified diving computer  with it being water resistant up to 100  meters compared to 50 on the other Apple  watch models and making it even better  the ultra Now features Precision dual  frequency GPS for Pinpoint location  tracking accuracy since L5 GPS is the  latest and greatest GPS signal available  to civilians helping the new Waypoint  marking and backtracking feature within  the redesigned compass work the best and  as an added bonus to all of that you  also get a new exclusive braided charger  in the Box to complete the premium feel  alongside the completely unique  outdoorsy packaging so with all that  said and out of the way it's time to get  into the question of if you should  actually upgrade to the ultra from a  previous Apple watch so let's get right  into that probably the most impressive  part about the Apple watch Ultra is the  fact that it's only 799 dollars while  coming with a premium titanium casing  and cellular already built in which is  kind of shocking because the previous 45  millimeter Series 7 model with a  titanium casing started at 849 dollars  even more expensive than the ultra and  to think that you're now getting a  larger 49 millimeter casing the new  redesign with an even more protected  display that is now twice as bright  literally double the battery life and  many other upgrades and features all for  less cash than a clearly inferior Series  7 model and not only that but I specced  up a new smaller 41 millimeter series 8  stainless steel model for my wife and  couldn't believe it ended up being 750  dollars only 50 bucks less than the  ultra so it actually ordered her an  ultra and planned to cancel the series  8. so in my opinion if you were thinking  of finally upgrading to one of the  series 8 models and choosing a nicer  metal material you should honestly just  buy the ultra instead if you care about  value however there is a bit of a caveat  and that's the fact that the ultra looks  absolutely massive on smaller wrists  like iJustine showed off at Apple's  events and that alone could be a deal  breaker for some people like my wife who  told me she didn't want a massive Apple  watch Ultra despite all of the extra  features and battery life so I guess I'm  just gonna end up keeping it for myself  so if you don't mind the big 49  millimeter casing I would recommend  upgrading hands down especially if  you're someone who really cares about  battery life that 36 hour battery alone  will seal the deal especially if you're  upgrading from an older Apple watch like  the series four or five where your  battery is likely getting old already  and there are even more feature changes  going up to the new Ultra and in my  honest opinion I feel like the ultra  combined with the way finder watch face  looks really unique and actually looks  more like a stylish high-end watch than  the pretty basic apple watches of the  past so if you're all about style the  ultra is where it's at and of course if  you do any type of sports and care about  that aspect of the watch you should 100  be buying this model if you can the only  reason I wouldn't recommend the ultra is  if you really don't care about having  cellular service the higher end titanium  material compared to aluminum or any of  the other feature and in that case you  can save a lot of money by going with  the 400 series 8 or even a renewed  Series 7 for as low as 320 on Amazon  using the link below but with all that  said what it all comes down to is this  the Apple watch Ultra is for people who  like the Apple watch and want the best  version that's it case closed so if  that's you you should definitely upgrade  to the ultra and let me know your  thoughts on if you're upgrading and  which model you're upgrading from down  in the comment section below definitely  check out the link below for the grid  Studio frames with the flash sale and  click subscribe because we are going to  be covering these new watches and the  ultra in detail very soon so definitely  subscribe thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next video  foreign
 

